# The host's HTTPS edge. Copy to deploy/edge/.env, fill in, and run
#   ./deploy/edge.sh --host=<ssh-target>
# The copy is gitignored because the names belong to one deployment, and this
# sample only ever carries example.org names.
#
# One Caddy per host serves every console that host publishes on its loopback,
# each under its own name, with a Let's Encrypt certificate per name. Caddy
# never reads this file: deploy/edge.sh turns it into deploy/edge/Caddyfile,
# one site per domain set here, and ships that. See "Public HTTPS: the host's
# edge" in deploy/README.md.
#
# An empty domain means that console is not served, so a host that runs only
# one of the two leaves the other empty. At least one must be set. A domain is
# a plain DNS name (no scheme, port or path) whose A record points at the host
# before the first run, and the host's ports 80 and 443 must be open to the
# internet.

# --- web2-admin console -----------------------------------------------------
# Optional. The name the web2-admin console is served at, e.g.
# admin.example.org. Empty: not served.
ADMIN_DOMAIN=

# Optional. The host loopback port that console is published on, which is
# what deploy/deploy.sh printed: 9090 by default, WEB2_ADMIN_WEB_PORT from the
# profile's env file, or 11009 + N*10 with --portSlot=<N>. Default: 9090.
ADMIN_PORT=9090

# --- streaming-infra-manager console ----------------------------------------
# Optional. The name the manager's console is served at, e.g.
# streaminfra.example.org. Empty: not served. Setting it does not deploy the
# manager, which has its own repository and deploy script.
#
# The manager's own manager/.env has a key of the same name. On a host that
# runs this edge, leave that one empty and put the name here instead: set
# there, it starts the manager's built-in edge, which wants the same ports 80
# and 443, and only one thing per host can have them.
MANAGER_DOMAIN=

# Optional. The host loopback port the manager's console is published on, its
# WEB_PORT. Default: 8080.
MANAGER_PORT=8080

# --- Let's Encrypt ----------------------------------------------------------
# Optional. The contact address on the Let's Encrypt account, for the rare
# notice that concerns it, such as a certificate that has to be revoked. It is
# not a renewal alarm: Caddy renews on its own, and Let's Encrypt stopped
# sending expiry reminders in 2025. With it set, Caddy also lists ZeroSSL as a
# second certificate authority to fall back on. Empty: certificates are issued
# all the same. Let's Encrypt refuses an address at example.com, example.net
# or example.org, and deploy/edge.sh refuses one too.
ACME_EMAIL=
